    "text": "To determine how many full glasses of juice Daniel can serve, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of juice Daniel has.\n2. Determine how many full glasses can be served with the total amount of juice.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total amount of juice Daniel has. He has 5 jars of juice, and each jar contains 2 liters. Since there are 1000 milliliters in a liter, each jar contains:\n\\[ 2 \\text{ liters} \\times 1000 \\text{ milliliters/liter} = 2000 \\text{ milliliters} \\]\nSo, the total amount of juice is:\n\\[ 5 \\text{ jars} \\times 2000 \\text{ milliliters/jar} = 10000 \\text{ milliliters} \\]\n\nNext, we need to determine how many full glasses of juice can be served. Each glass can hold up to 250 milliliters of juice. Therefore, the number of full glasses that can be served is:\n\\[ \\frac{10000 \\text{ milliliters}}{250 \\text{ milliliters/glass}} = 40 \\text{ glasses} \\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{40} \\]",
